{:href "/athletes/80777"} "Stien Baas-Kaiser"] " " [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"] " / 12 February 1972 / " [:a {:href "/records/event_name/540"} "Details"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Starter"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/99265"} "Manfred Zojer"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUT.png"}] "AUT"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Referee"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/1200586"} "Jean Heckly"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "At the 1975 World Championships, the distance had been won by Dutch skater " [:a {:href "/athletes/82867"} "Sippie Tigchelaar"] ", who was not in Innsbruck because of disputes with the Dutch national team. Second was East Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/81475"} "Karin Kessow"] ", who won the all-around, followed by Soviet skater, " [:a {:href "/athletes/80567"} "Tatyana Averina"] ", who had already won the 1,000 in Innsbruck. The world record had been set by Tamara Kuznetsova at Medeo in 1975, but she was also not at the 1976 Winter Olympics."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the first pair East German " [:a {:href "/athletes/80606"} "Ines Bautzmann"] " broke the Olympic record with 4:46.67. Averina was in the sixth pair and moved ahead, posting 4:45.19, narrowly above the world record of 4:44.69, and three seconds better than her PB. Three pairs later Norway’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/80639"} "Lisbeth Korsmo"] " was right on Averina’s pace for most of the race only to miss out by a tantalizingly close margin, 4:45.24 – only 5/100ths of a second back. In the 10th pair, East German " [:a {:href "/athletes/81847"} "Andrea Mitscherlich"] " was even closer, finishing in 4:45.23, especially fast when one considers that Mitscherlich had only recently turned 15-years-old. Kessow was up in the final pair, the 13th. She skated well, and was never much off the leading pace, finishing in 4:45.60. Remarkably the four top skaters were within 41/100ths of a second."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Averina was the top female skater at the 1976 Winter Olympics. She won two gold medals and two bronze medals in the four events. This was her first ever victory in a 3,000 at a major meet, as early in her career, she had primarily been considered a sprinter. Averina would win the 1978 World Championships."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button381652", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button381652').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "200 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "600 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "1000 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "1400 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "1800 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "2200 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "2600 m"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "6I"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/80567"} "Tatyana Averina"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "4:45.19"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "21.43"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "57.74"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "1:34.28"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "2:11.83"] [:td {:class "split", :